    <!-- iOS ProgressTab grammarContent (range × accuracy ceiling). -->
    <string name="grammar_measures_two_reads">Two reads, the lower wins: the structures you actually build in a talk, and transcript-verified slips per 100 words — STT artifacts and style suggestions excluded. Short correct sentences read low, not high.</string>
    <string name="grammar_improve_longer_sentences">Say more in one sentence — a reason, a condition, what happened before. Longer sentences are what move this band.</string>
    <string name="grammar_trend_caption_ceiling">Verified slips per 100 words, one point per talk — your accuracy. The band above comes from the structures you build, so this curve alone can’t move it.</string>
